<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stockholms Banco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1657">1657</a>–<a href="/years/1668">1668</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Palmstruch Bank</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholms</a> Banco was a Swedish bank founded by Johan Palmstruch in 1657 under royal charter. In 1661 it issued the first banknotes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, credit notes that could be exchanged for heavy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> plate money. It issued more notes than it could redeem and collapsed in the late 1660s, and in 1668 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riksdag">Riksdag</a> replaced it with the Bank of the Estates of the Realm, today's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sveriges-riksbank">Sveriges Riksbank</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stockholms-banco.jpg" alt="Stockholms Banco" width="320" height="262" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SVERIGES RIKSBANK · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kreditivsedel_1661.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
